  <h3>Product</h3>

  <p>The acquisition left at least five separately built products across divisions, and the brand had to reach into them or it wasn't a brand. I built the shared visual language through skinning and concept work, designing in Sketch and writing the HTML and CSS against engineering's React components myself, on variables throughout, before &ldquo;tokens&rdquo; was the word for it.</p>

  <p>The first product I applied it to was the in-cab ELD, the LV-9000 driver terminal: an embedded device with a fixed display, a driver who can't be looking at it, and DOT rules about what has to be on screen. Brand type, color, and the graphic-element vocabulary, applied under constraints a marketing page never has. I designed and handed off the reskin to the ELD engineering team in 2020.</p>

  <figure>
    <%= image_tag "work/powerfleet_rebrand/eld-lv9000-home.png", loading: :lazy, alt: "LV-9000 in-cab ELD home screen in the PowerFleet brand" %>
    <figcaption>
      <p>
        LV-9000 in-cab ELD, home screen. Brand type, color, and the callout vocabulary on a fixed embedded display.
      </p>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>The full Connect platform reskin didn't ship before the company's direction changed, but the language did: it became the <%= link_to "Intermodal concept", "/work/powerfleet-chassis" %> in 2021 and the basis for the Unity refresh in 2022.</p>

